  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The outbox is a Room table",
      "items": [
        "the mutation and the intent to send it commit together: the outbox is persisted in Room, never in memory",
        "the row carries an idempotency key, so a retry after a crash cannot apply the change twice",
        "a fire-and-forget mutation with no idempotency key and no rollback is a review finding \u2014 the fixed version writes the Room outbox and lets WorkManager drain it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "WorkManager is the scheduler",
      "items": [
        "WorkManager is for deferrable guaranteed work \u2014 the outbox drain, uploads; a foreground service only where policy allows",
        "constraints and backoff are the retry policy; WorkManagerTestInitHelper is how the idempotency and the retry are proven",
        "the drain reads the pending rows and posts them; the server is authoritative for game state, prices, payments and entitlements"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Conflicts and death",
      "items": [
        "a conflict is resolved by the server; the local pending change is rejected visibly, never silently dropped",
        "backoff, then a dead-letter view \u2014 the user sees what did not sync instead of a spinner that never ends",
        "clear user data on sign-out or tenant switch, pending outbox rows included"
      ]
    }
  ]
